INSERT INTO `case_document_chunks` VALUES (1,1,1,1,0,'CASE RECORD: Apex Global Logistics v. QuickFreight Multi-Modal Logistics Pvt Ltd (Comm. O.S. No. 481/2026). Document: Plaint_with_Statement_of_Truth_Apex_Comm_OS_481.pdf. Court: City Civil & Commercial Court, Bengaluru. Matter involving commercial dispute and evidentiary submissions under Indian Practice OS.','[\"case\", \"record\", \"apex\", \"global\", \"logistics\", \"quickfreight\", \"multi\", \"modal\", \"logistics\", \"pvt\", \"ltd\", \"comm\", \"481\", \"2026\", \"document\", \"plaint\", \"statement\", \"truth\", \"apex\", \"comm\", \"481\", \"pdf\", \"court\", \"city\", \"civil\", \"commercial\", \"court\", \"bengaluru\", \"matter\", \"involving\", \"commercial\", \"dispute\", \"evidentiary\", \"submissions\", \"indian\", \"practice\"]','[\"Apex Global Logistics\", \"Modal Logistics Pvt Ltd\", \"City Civil\", \"Commercial Court\", \"Indian Practice\"]','[]','2026-10-08 12:07:45'),(2,1,1,2,0,'CASE RECORD: Apex Global Logistics v. QuickFreight Multi-Modal Logistics Pvt Ltd (Comm. O.S. No. 481/2026). Document: Master_MultiModal_Transport_Agreement_2025.pdf. Court: City Civil & Commercial Court, Bengaluru. Matter involving commercial dispute and evidentiary submissions under Indian Practice OS.','[\"case\", \"record\", \"apex\", \"global\", \"logistics\", \"quickfreight\", \"multi\", \"modal\", \"logistics\", \"pvt\", \"ltd\", \"comm\", \"481\", \"2026\", \"document\", \"master\", \"multimodal\", \"transport\", \"agreement\", \"2025\", \"pdf\", \"court\", \"city\", \"civil\", \"commercial\", \"court\", \"bengaluru\", \"matter\", \"involving\", \"commercial\", \"dispute\", \"evidentiary\", \"submissions\", \"indian\", \"practice\"]','[\"Apex Global Logistics\", \"Modal Logistics Pvt Ltd\", \"City Civil\", \"Commercial Court\", \"Indian Practice\"]','[]','2026-10-08 12:08:08'),(3,1,1,8,0,'I T W I N E T E C H N O L O G I E S · A I I N I T I A T I V E Claude Certification Test Booklet The starting test, Team Tests #1 to #5, and how to build the Gateway Test Companion to the Claude Certification Study Plan Answers are in the separate Answer Key document Questions in total 125 Written by Subodh · iTWINE Technologies Version 28 September 2026 · starts Tuesday 29 September 6 tests Every question topic-tagged No answers in this document THESE ARE PRACTICE QUESTIONS, NOT REAL EXAM QUESTIONS Nobody outside Anthropic has the real questions. These are written for iTWINE from the published topic list, in the same style, so that practising on them builds the right habits and shows you which topics you are weak in.','[\"claude\", \"certification\", \"test\", \"booklet\", \"starting\", \"test\", \"team\", \"tests\", \"build\", \"gateway\", \"test\", \"companion\", \"claude\", \"certification\", \"study\", \"plan\", \"answers\", \"separate\", \"answer\", \"key\", \"document\", \"questions\", \"total\", \"125\", \"written\", \"subodh\", \"itwine\", \"technologies\", \"version\", \"september\", \"2026\", \"starts\", \"tuesday\", \"september\", \"tests\", \"every\", \"question\", \"topic\", \"tagged\", \"answers\", \"document\", \"practice\", \"questions\", \"real\", \"exam\", \"questions\", \"nobody\", \"outside\", \"anthropic\", \"real\", \"questions\", \"written\", \"itwine\", \"published\", \"topic\", \"list\", \"style\", \"practising\", \"builds\", \"right\", \"habits\", \"shows\", \"topics\", \"weak\"]','[\"Claude Certification Test Booklet The\", \"Team Tests\", \"Gateway Test Companion\", \"Claude Certification Study Plan Answers\", \"Answer Key\"]','[\"28 September 2026\", \"29 September\"]','2026-10-08 12:12:06'),(4,1,1,8,1,'Section 1 How to run a timed test The short answer: Google Forms is the right tool for five of these tests and the wrong tool for one of them. Here is why, and what to use instead. What the real exam is like The real exam does this Why it matters for practice Hard 120-minute limit About 2 minutes per question. Running out of time is a common way to fail, and you can only learn pacing by practising against a clock. Closed book, no notes, no AI If you can look things up, the score tells you nothing. Locks your browser and watches you You cannot open another tab. No free tool copies this, and we should not try. Lets you flag a question and come back Answer the easy ones first, mark the hard ones, return at the end. Tells you how many answers to pick on multi- answer questions Use that number to check your reasoning. Gives a score per topic afterwards The most useful part of the result. Our tests must do the same. What Google Forms can and cannot do Need Google Forms alone Notes Auto-marking Yes Turn on \"Make this a quiz\" in Settings, then set the correct answer and points on each question. Results exported for analysis Yes Link the form to a Google Sheet. This is how you get a score per topic. Shuffle question and option order Yes So people cannot compare answers by position. Go back and change an answer Yes Only if you keep all questions on one page. Countdown timer No Forms was built for surveys. There is no clock and no auto-submit. Auto-submit when time runs out No Without this, a time limit is only a suggestion. Everyone starts at the same moment No Not without an add-on that opens the form at a set time. Stop people opening another tab No No free tool does this properly. Solve it by being in the same room. The three gaps that matter — timer, auto-submit and a common start time — are fixed by a free Google Forms add-on. Search the Google Workspace Marketplace for \"timer for Google Forms\". Install one, test it on yourself before 7 October, and check the free plan covers the number of people we have. The Starting Test needs no timer, so tomorrow\'s test does not depend on this. What to use for each test Test Use this Why Starting test 29 Sep Google Forms, no timer needed The point is measuring what people already know, not pressure. Let people take the twenty minutes they need. iTWINE Technologies · Claude Certification Test Booklet 2 / 19','[\"section\", \"run\", \"timed\", \"test\", \"short\", \"answer\", \"google\", \"forms\", \"right\", \"tool\", \"five\", \"tests\", \"wrong\", \"tool\", \"one\", \"use\", \"instead\", \"real\", \"exam\", \"like\", \"real\", \"exam\", \"matters\", \"practice\", \"hard\", \"120\", \"minute\", \"limit\", \"minutes\", \"per\", \"question\", \"running\", \"time\", \"common\", \"way\", \"fail\", \"learn\", \"pacing\", \"practising\", \"clock\", \"closed\", \"book\", \"notes\", \"look\", \"things\", \"score\", \"tells\", \"nothing\", \"locks\", \"browser\", \"watches\", \"open\", \"another\", \"tab\", \"free\", \"tool\", \"copies\", \"try\", \"lets\", \"flag\", \"question\", \"come\", \"back\", \"answer\", \"easy\", \"ones\", \"first\", \"mark\", \"hard\", \"ones\", \"return\", \"end\", \"tells\", \"many\", \"answers\", \"pick\", \"multi\", \"answer\", \"questions\", \"use\", \"number\", \"check\", \"reasoning\", \"gives\", \"score\", \"per\", \"topic\", \"afterwards\", \"useful\", \"part\", \"result\", \"tests\", \"must\", \"google\", \"forms\", \"need\", \"google\", \"forms\", \"alone\", \"notes\", \"auto\", \"marking\", \"yes\", \"turn\", \"make\", \"quiz\", \"settings\", \"set\", \"correct\", \"answer\", \"points\", \"question\", \"results\", \"exported\", \"analysis\", \"yes\", \"link\", \"form\", \"google\", \"sheet\", \"get\", \"score\", \"per\", \"topic\", \"shuffle\", \"question\", \"option\", \"order\", \"yes\", \"people\", \"compare\", \"answers\", \"position\", \"back\", \"change\", \"answer\", \"yes\", \"keep\", \"questions\", \"one\", \"page\", \"countdown\", \"timer\", \"forms\", \"built\", \"surveys\", \"clock\", \"auto\", \"submit\", \"auto\", \"submit\", \"time\", \"runs\", \"without\", \"time\", \"limit\", \"suggestion\", \"everyone\", \"starts\", \"moment\", \"without\", \"add\", \"opens\", \"form\", \"set\", \"time\", \"stop\", \"people\", \"opening\", \"another\", \"tab\", \"free\", \"tool\", \"properly\", \"solve\", \"room\", \"three\", \"gaps\", \"matter\", \"timer\", \"auto\", \"submit\", \"common\", \"start\", \"time\", \"fixed\", \"free\", \"google\", \"forms\", \"add\", \"search\", \"google\", \"workspace\", \"marketplace\", \"timer\", \"google\", \"forms\", \"install\", \"one\", \"test\", \"october\", \"check\", \"free\", \"plan\", \"covers\", \"number\", \"people\", \"starting\", \"test\", \"needs\", \"timer\", \"tomorrow\", \"test\", \"depend\", \"use\", \"test\", \"test\", \"use\", \"starting\", \"test\", \"sep\", \"google\", \"forms\", \"timer\", \"needed\", \"point\", \"measuring\", \"people\", \"already\", \"know\", \"pressure\", \"let\", \"people\", \"take\", \"twenty\", \"minutes\", \"need\", \"itwine\", \"technologies\", \"claude\", \"certification\", \"test\", \"booklet\"]','[\"Google Forms\", \"What Google Forms\", \"Need Google Forms\", \"Notes Auto\", \"Yes Turn\"]','[\"7 October\", \"29 Sep\"]','2026-10-08 12:12:06'),(5,1,1,8,2,'Test Use this Why Team Tests #1 to #5 Google Forms + a timer add-on, 30 minutes The point is finding weak topics. Auto-marking and the Sheet export are what you need. Daily 10-minute revision This paper booklet Your partner reads the question out loud. Saying an answer out loud is harder than clicking one. Practice exam 18 Nov The Anthropic Partner Academy The closest thing to the real exam that exists. Do not rebuild it in Forms. Book 11:00 to 13:30. Gateway Test 23 Nov and 1 Dec Printed on paper, in one room, with a clock on the wall This is a decision, not a study aid. Paper removes the browser entirely. Marking fifty questions by hand takes about ten minutes per person and is worth it. IF YOU WOULD RATHER RUN THE GATEWAY TEST IN FORMS That is fine. Use the timer add-on set to 90 minutes with auto-submit, put everyone in the same room at the same time, phones face down, laptops showing nothing but the form. The room matters more than the tool. Do not send the link out and let people take it at their desks whenever they like — that measures nothing. iTWINE Technologies · Claude Certification Test Booklet 3 / 19','[\"test\", \"use\", \"team\", \"tests\", \"google\", \"forms\", \"timer\", \"add\", \"minutes\", \"point\", \"finding\", \"weak\", \"topics\", \"auto\", \"marking\", \"sheet\", \"export\", \"need\", \"daily\", \"minute\", \"revision\", \"paper\", \"booklet\", \"partner\", \"reads\", \"question\", \"loud\", \"saying\", \"answer\", \"loud\", \"harder\", \"clicking\", \"one\", \"practice\", \"exam\", \"nov\", \"anthropic\", \"partner\", \"academy\", \"closest\", \"thing\", \"real\", \"exam\", \"exists\", \"rebuild\", \"forms\", \"book\", \"gateway\", \"test\", \"nov\", \"dec\", \"printed\", \"paper\", \"one\", \"room\", \"clock\", \"wall\", \"decision\", \"study\", \"aid\", \"paper\", \"removes\", \"browser\", \"entirely\", \"marking\", \"fifty\", \"questions\", \"hand\", \"takes\", \"ten\", \"minutes\", \"per\", \"person\", \"worth\", \"rather\", \"run\", \"gateway\", \"test\", \"forms\", \"fine\", \"use\", \"timer\", \"add\", \"set\", \"minutes\", \"auto\", \"submit\", \"put\", \"everyone\", \"room\", \"time\", \"phones\", \"face\", \"laptops\", \"showing\", \"nothing\", \"form\", \"room\", \"matters\", \"tool\", \"send\", \"link\", \"let\", \"people\", \"take\", \"desks\", \"whenever\", \"like\", \"measures\", \"nothing\", \"itwine\", \"technologies\", \"claude\", \"certification\", \"test\", \"booklet\"]','[\"Test Use\", \"Why Team Tests\", \"Google Forms\", \"Nov The Anthropic Partner Academy The\", \"Gateway Test\"]','[\"18 Nov\", \"23 Nov\", \"1 Dec\"]','2026-10-08 12:12:07'),(6,1,1,8,3,'Section 2 Setting up the tests Today (28 September): build the Starting Test form only, so tomorrow\'s test can run. Build the other five forms before 7 October, so Test #1 can run on 8 October. ITWINE HAS NO GOOGLE WORKSPACE — RESTRICT THE EMAIL FIELD INSTEAD Without a company domain, Forms cannot limit who can respond by account. Add a response-validation rule on the email question: first make the email question a Short answer question, marked Required, and put it first. Then click the three dots on it, choose Response validation → Regular expression → Matches, paste the pattern below, and add a custom error message telling people to re-check their address. (Do not use the \"Collect email addresses\" setting for this: it does not use the pattern.) ^[A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@yourcompany\\.com$ This is a typo check, not real authentication. It stops a mistyped address from silently going nowhere — nothing more. It does not stop someone typing a colleague\'s correct address, and it does not prove who clicked submit. The real integrity control is unchanged: same room, phones face down, on the clock, marked as a group. Use the email answer as the row label in the results Sheet so topic scores land against the right name. On test day Create one Google Form per test. Six forms in total. Name them clearly: Claude Cert — Starting Test, Claude Cert — Test 1, and so on. 1 Turn on quiz mode on all six. Settings, then \"Make this a quiz\". Starting Test only: set \"Release grades\" to Immediately after each submission. It is ungated and individual — the trainee needs their score and weakest topic the same day to fill in the Day 1 exit ticket. Tests #1 to #5: set \"Release grades\" to Later, after manual review, so nobody sees a score until everyone has finished and you are ready to go through the wrong answers together. 2 ◦ ◦ Type in the questions from Sections 3 to 5 of this booklet. Multiple choice, one answer, four options each. Keep them all on one page so people can scroll back and change answers. 3 Set the correct answer and 1 point on every question, from the Answer Key document. 4 Add the topic label. This is the step people skip and then regret. The label is printed next to every question, for example DEV- D2 . Put it in the question\'s \"Answer feedback\" field, or keep a lookup table in the results Sheet mapping question number to topic. Without it you cannot tell anyone which topic they are weak in. 5 Turn on \"Shuffle option order\" in Presentation settings. Leave question order alone so the topic labels still line up. 6 Link the form to a Google Sheet (Responses tab, the Sheets icon). Add a tab called Topic scores with one column per topic, and a formula that counts correct answers per topic for each person. 7 Install a timer add-on and test it on yourself. Set 30 minutes for Tests #1 to #5. 8 Print the Gateway Test on paper in the week beginning 16 November, once you have built it using Section 8. 9 Everyone in the same room, at the same time. 1 Phones face down on the table. No notes, no documentation, no AI help. 2 Start the timer. Nobody starts early. 3 iTWINE Technologies · Claude Certification Test Booklet 4 / 19','[\"section\", \"setting\", \"tests\", \"today\", \"september\", \"build\", \"starting\", \"test\", \"form\", \"tomorrow\", \"test\", \"run\", \"build\", \"five\", \"forms\", \"october\", \"test\", \"run\", \"october\", \"itwine\", \"google\", \"workspace\", \"restrict\", \"email\", \"field\", \"instead\", \"without\", \"company\", \"domain\", \"forms\", \"limit\", \"respond\", \"account\", \"add\", \"response\", \"validation\", \"rule\", \"email\", \"question\", \"first\", \"make\", \"email\", \"question\", \"short\", \"answer\", \"question\", \"marked\", \"required\", \"put\", \"first\", \"click\", \"three\", \"dots\", \"choose\", \"response\", \"validation\", \"regular\", \"expression\", \"matches\", \"paste\", \"pattern\", \"add\", \"custom\", \"error\", \"message\", \"telling\", \"people\", \"check\", \"address\", \"use\", \"collect\", \"email\", \"addresses\", \"setting\", \"use\", \"pattern\", \"yourcompany\", \"com\", \"typo\", \"check\", \"real\", \"authentication\", \"stops\", \"mistyped\", \"address\", \"silently\", \"going\", \"nowhere\", \"nothing\", \"stop\", \"someone\", \"typing\", \"colleague\", \"correct\", \"address\", \"prove\", \"clicked\", \"submit\", \"real\", \"integrity\", \"control\", \"un