swers\", \"per\", \"topic\", \"person\", \"install\", \"timer\", \"add\", \"test\", \"set\", \"minutes\", \"tests\", \"print\", \"gateway\", \"test\", \"paper\", \"week\", \"beginning\", \"november\", \"built\", \"using\", \"section\", \"everyone\", \"room\", \"time\", \"phones\", \"face\", \"table\", \"notes\", \"documentation\", \"help\", \"start\", \"timer\", \"nobody\", \"starts\", \"early\", \"itwine\", \"technologies\", \"claude\", \"certification\", \"test\", \"booklet\"]','[\"Starting Test\", \"Google Form\", \"Claude Cert\", \"Answer Key\", \"Google Sheet\"]','[\"28 September\", \"7 October\", \"8 October\", \"16 November\"]','2026-10-08 12:12:07'),(7,1,1,8,4,'THE ONE RULE THAT MAKES ALL OF THIS WORTHWHILE A total score tells you almost nothing. \"You got 14 out of 20\" leads nowhere. \"You got 3 out of 6 on Applications and Integration, which is a third of your exam\" tells you exactly what to do next. Record the topic scores every time. When everyone has finished, release the grades and go through every wrong answer as a group. The Answer Key gives the reason. The documentation gives the detail. Find both. 4 Record each person\'s score per topic in the shared folder, not just the total. By Test #5 you should be able to draw a line per topic and watch it climb. 5 iTWINE Technologies · Claude Certification Test Booklet 5 / 19','[\"one\", \"rule\", \"makes\", \"worthwhile\", \"total\", \"score\", \"tells\", \"almost\", \"nothing\", \"got\", \"leads\", \"nowhere\", \"got\", \"applications\", \"integration\", \"third\", \"exam\", \"tells\", \"exactly\", \"next\", \"record\", \"topic\", \"scores\", \"every\", \"time\", \"everyone\", \"finished\", \"release\", \"grades\", \"every\", \"wrong\", \"answer\", \"group\", \"answer\", \"key\", \"gives\", \"reason\", \"documentation\", \"gives\", \"detail\", \"find\", \"record\", \"person\", \"score\", \"per\", \"topic\", \"shared\", \"folder\", \"just\", \"total\", \"test\", \"able\", \"draw\", \"line\", \"per\", \"topic\", \"watch\", \"climb\", \"itwine\", \"technologies\", \"claude\", \"certification\", \"test\", \"booklet\"]','[\"The Answer Key\", \"By Test\", \"Claude Certification Test Booklet\"]','[]','2026-10-08 12:12:07'),(8,1,1,8,5,'Section 3 The starting test Twenty questions, taken on Tuesday 29 September. No notes. About twenty minutes. No time limit needed. THIS TEST DOES NOT GO ON YOUR RECORD Its only job is to show how much study time you need. Someone who already builds with Claude may need half the hours in the plan. Someone new may need more. A low score today changes your study plan, not your reputation. The Form releases your score the moment you submit — you should know your weakest topic before the day is over. 1 What is a token? D5 A) One letter B) About three quarters of an English word C) One full sentence D) One API call 2 What does the context window include? D5 A) Only the text you send B) Only Claude\'s reply C) Both what you send and what comes back D) Only the system prompt 3 Which Claude model family is built to be fastest and cheapest? D5 A) Opus B) Sonnet C) Haiku D) They all cost the same 4 The Claude API is stateless. What does that mean for a long conversation? D2 A) It cannot use tools B) You must send the whole history on every call C) It only works offline D) It cannot stream 5 Where do instructions that set Claude\'s role and limits belong? D6 A) In the tool schema B) In the URL C) In the last user message D) In the system prompt 6 What does stop_reason tell you? D4 A) Why Claude stopped writing B) How many tokens you used C) Which model answered D) The cost of the call 7 An HTTP 429 error means: D4 A) Your JSON is broken B) Your key is wrong C) You sent too many requests D) The model name is wrong 8 In tool use, who actually runs the function? D8 A) Claude B) Anthropic\'s servers C) Your own program D) The MCP registry 9 In MCP, which side provides the tools and data? D8 A) The client B) The server C) Both equally D) Neither; the model does 10 What is prompt caching for? D5 A) Reusing repeated prompt text to cut cost and time B) Saving replies to disk C) Remembering past conversations D) Storing user passwords 11 What is prompt injection? D7 A) Adding examples to a prompt B) Sending two prompts at once C) A caching error D) Hidden instructions inside data that try to change Claude\'s behaviour 12 Which normally costs more per token? D5 A) Input tokens B) Output tokens C) They are always equal D) It depends on the time of day 13 What is an eval? D4 A) A pricing report B) A type of prompt C) An automatic test for model output D) A logging tool 14 What does is_error: true on a tool_result do? D4 A) Ends the conversation B) Tells Claude the tool failed, so it can recover C) Retries the tool automatically D) Writes to the console 15 You have 5,000 documents to process overnight and nobody is waiting. What is cheapest? D2 A) Live calls, one at a time B) The Message Batches API C) Streaming D) Extended thinking iTWINE Technologies · Claude Certification Test Booklet 6 / 19','[\"section\", \"starting\", \"test\", \"twenty\", \"questions\", \"taken\", \"tuesday\", \"september\", \"notes\", \"twenty\", \"minutes\", \"time\", \"limit\", \"needed\", \"test\", \"record\", \"job\", \"show\", \"much\", \"study\", \"time\", \"need\", \"someone\", \"already\", \"builds\", \"claude\", \"may\", \"need\", \"half\", \"hours\", \"plan\", \"someone\", \"new\", \"may\", \"need\", \"low\", \"score\", \"today\", \"changes\", \"study\", \"plan\", \"reputation\", \"form\", \"releases\", \"score\", \"moment\", \"submit\", \"know\", \"weakest\", \"topic\", \"day\", \"token\", \"one\", \"letter\", \"three\", \"quarters\", \"english\", \"word\", \"one\", \"full\", \"sentence\", \"one\", \"api\", \"call\", \"context\", \"window\", \"include\", \"text\", \"send\", \"claude\", \"reply\", \"send\", \"comes\", \"back\", \"system\", \"prompt\", \"claude\", \"model\", \"family\", \"built\", \"fastest\", \"cheapest\", \"opus\", \"sonnet\", \"haiku\", \"cost\", \"claude\", \"api\", \"stateless\", \"mean\", \"long\", \"conversation\", \"use\", \"tools\", \"must\", \"send\", \"whole\", \"history\", \"every\", \"call\", \"works\", \"offline\", \"stream\", \"instructions\", \"set\", \"claude\", \"role\", \"limits\", \"belong\", \"tool\", \"schema\", \"url\", \"last\", \"user\", \"message\", \"system\", \"prompt\", \"stop\", \"reason\", \"tell\", \"claude\", \"stopped\", \"writing\", \"many\", \"tokens\", \"used\", \"model\", \"answered\", \"cost\", \"call\", \"http\", \"429\", \"error\", \"means\", \"json\", \"broken\", \"key\", \"wrong\", \"sent\", \"many\", \"requests\", \"model\", \"name\", \"wrong\", \"tool\", \"use\", \"actually\", \"runs\", \"function\", \"claude\", \"anthropic\", \"servers\", \"program\", \"mcp\", \"registry\", \"mcp\", \"side\", \"provides\", \"tools\", \"data\", \"client\", \"server\", \"equally\", \"neither\", \"model\", \"prompt\", \"caching\", \"reusing\", \"repeated\", \"prompt\", \"text\", \"cut\", \"cost\", \"time\", \"saving\", \"replies\", \"disk\", \"remembering\", \"past\", \"conversations\", \"storing\", \"user\", \"passwords\", \"prompt\", \"injection\", \"adding\", \"examples\", \"prompt\", \"sending\", \"two\", \"prompts\", \"caching\", \"error\", \"hidden\", \"instructions\", \"inside\", \"data\", \"try\", \"change\", \"claude\", \"behaviour\", \"normally\", \"costs\", \"per\", \"token\", \"input\", \"tokens\", \"output\", \"tokens\", \"always\", \"equal\", \"depends\", \"time\", \"day\", \"eval\", \"pricing\", \"report\", \"type\", \"prompt\", \"automatic\", \"test\", \"model\", \"output\", \"logging\", \"tool\", \"error\", \"true\", \"tool\", \"result\", \"ends\", \"conversation\", \"tells\", \"claude\", \"tool\", \"failed\", \"recover\", \"retries\", \"tool\", \"automatically\", \"writes\", \"console\", \"000\", \"documents\", \"process\", \"overnight\", \"nobody\", \"waiting\", \"cheapest\", \"live\", \"calls\", \"one\", \"time\", \"message\", \"batches\", \"api\", \"streaming\", \"extended\", \"thinking\", \"itwine\", \"technologies\", \"claude\", \"certification\", \"test\", \"booklet\"]','[\"The Form\", \"Only Claude\", \"Which Claude\", \"The Claude\", \"Why Claude\"]','[\"29 September\"]','2026-10-08 12:12:08'),(9,1,1,8,6,'16 What is a hallucination? D7 A) A network error B) A refused request C) The model stating something untrue with confidence D) A cache miss 17 Where should an API key be stored? D7 A) In the source code B) In a .env file that is never committed to Git C) In the project README D) In a team chat message 18 What does \"few-shot\" mean? D6 A) Putting example inputs and outputs inside the prompt B) Using a small model C) Setting a low max_tokens D) Sending very few requests 19 What is the Agent SDK for? D1 A) Designing databases B) Writing SQL C) Managing invoices D) Building agents: the loop, subagents, hooks and tools 20 An HTTP 400 error usually means: D4 A) The server is down B) Something is wrong with your request, often the JSON or the tool schema C) You sent too many requests D) Your key expired What your score means Score What to do 16–20 You already know the basics. Do all the Core tasks anyway, but spend most of your Stretch time on your track\'s two biggest topics from the start. You may only need 20 to 25 hours in total. 10–15 You are exactly where this plan expects you to be. Follow it as written, Core and Stretch. Below 10 Nothing is wrong. You need more hours than the plan gives, so add 30 minutes a day of your own, and tell Subodh so your partner is someone who scored higher. Start with the free courses at anthropic.skilljar.com. iTWINE Technologies · Claude Certification Test Booklet 7 / 19','[\"hallucination\", \"network\", \"error\", \"refused\", \"request\", \"model\", \"stating\", \"something\", \"untrue\", \"confidence\", \"cache\", \"miss\", \"api\", \"key\", \"stored\", \"source\", \"code\", \"env\", \"file\", \"never\", \"committed\", \"git\", \"project\", \"readme\", \"team\", \"chat\", \"message\", \"shot\", \"mean\", \"putting\", \"example\", \"inputs\", \"outputs\", \"inside\", \"prompt\", \"using\", \"small\", \"model\", \"setting\", \"low\", \"max\", \"tokens\", \"sending\", \"requests\", \"agent\", \"sdk\", \"designing\", \"databases\", \"writing\", \"sql\", \"managing\", \"invoices\", \"building\", \"agents\", \"loop\", \"subagents\", \"hooks\", \"tools\", \"http\", \"400\", \"error\", \"usually\", \"means\", \"server\", \"something\", \"wrong\", \"request\", \"often\", \"json\", \"tool\", \"schema\", \"sent\", \"many\", \"requests\", \"key\", \"expired\", \"score\", \"means\", \"score\", \"already\", \"know\", \"basics\", \"core\", \"tasks\", \"anyway\", \"spend\", \"stretch\", \"time\", \"track\", \"two\", \"biggest\", \"topics\", \"start\", \"may\", \"need\", \"hours\", \"total\", \"exactly\", \"plan\", \"expects\", \"follow\", \"written\", \"core\", \"stretch\", \"nothing\", \"wrong\", \"need\", \"hours\", \"plan\", \"gives\", \"add\", \"minutes\", \"day\", \"tell\", \"subodh\", \"partner\", \"someone\", \"scored\", \"higher\", \"start\", \"free\", \"courses\", \"anthropic\", \"skilljar\", \"com\", \"itwine\", \"technologies\", \"claude\", \"certification\", \"test\", \"booklet\"]','[\"Score What\", \"Claude Certification Test Booklet\"]','[]','2026-10-08 12:12:08'),(10,1,1,8,7,'Section 4 Team Tests #1 to #3 Twenty questions each. Thirty minutes. Also use these for the ten-minute revision at 11:00 every day: your partner reads out a question and the options, and you answer without notes. Test #1 · Thursday 8 October · Models, the API, system prompts, key words 1 A client needs a classifier that runs on 50,000 emails a day and must reply in under a second. Which model family fits best? DEV D5 A) Haiku B) Sonnet C) Opus D) Any of them; only the prompt matters 2 You must justify a model choice to a client. Which three things should your reason cover? DEV D5 A) Quality, latency, cost B) Quality, popularity, age C) Cost, colour, region D) Latency, brand, licence 3 Your script has used the same hardcoded model name for a year and suddenly returns 404. What is the most likely cause? DEV D5 A) The API key expired B) The model name is retired or misspelled C) You hit the rate limit D) The JSON is malformed 4 Which field in the reply tells you how many tokens the call used? DEV D2 A) content B) stop_reason C) usage D) id 5 A user complains that Claude\'s answer stopped in the middle of a sentence. Which field should you check first? DEV D4 A) usage.input_tokens B) stop_reason C) model D) role 6 Where is the conversation history stored between API calls? ARCH D1 A) On Anthropic\'s servers B) In the API key C) In your own application D) In the model weights 7 You want Claude to stay in one narrow role for a whole conversation. Where does that instruction belong? DEV D6 A) Repeated in every user message B) In the system prompt C) In the tool description D) In the HTTP header 8 You copy a tutorial that sets temperature: 0.1 and the request is rejected. What is the most likely reason? DEV D5 A) The value must be a whole number B) Temperature only works with tools C) Your model does not accept that setting D) You must also set top_k 9 Which pair of settings should you not tune together? DEV D5 A) temperature and top_p B) max_tokens and model C) system and messages D) stream and tools 10 Roughly how many tokens is a 400-word document? DEV D5 A) About 100 B) About 400 C) About 530 D) About 4,000 11 Your monthly bill is higher than expected and the input volume has not changed. What should you check first? DEV D5 A) The number of output tokens B) The colour of the dashboard C) The number of API keys D) The region 12 What is the correct order of the messages array for a three-turn conversation? DEV D2 A) All user turns, then all assistant turns B) Alternating user and assistant, oldest first C) Newest first D) Order does not matter 13 A junior developer puts the API key directly in main.py \"just for testing\". What is the first thing you tell them? DEV D7 A) It is fine if the repository is private B) Move it to .env and add .env to .gitignore C) Rename the variable D) Add a comment saying it is temporary 14 Which of these is not something the system prompt should contain? DEV D6 A) The assistant\'s role B) Output formatting rules C) Topics it must refuse D) The user\'s current question 15 A client asks why they cannot just use Opus for everything. What is the strongest answer? DEV D5 A) Opus is less accurate B) Opus cannot use tools C) Most tasks do not need it, and it costs and takes far more for no gain D) Opus is only for research iTWINE Technologies · Claude Certification Test Booklet 8 / 19','[\"section\", \"team\", \"tests\", \"twenty\", \"questions\", \"thirty\", \"minutes\", \"also\", \"use\", \"ten\", \"minute\", \"revision\", \"every\", \"day\", \"partner\", \"reads\", \"question\", \"options\", \"answer\", \"without\", \"notes\", \"test\", \"thursday\", \"october\", \"models\", \"api\", \"system\", \"prompts\", \"key\", \"words\", \"client\", \"needs\", \"classifier\", \"runs\", \"000\", \"emails\", \"day\", \"must\", \"reply\", \"second\", \"model\", \"family\", \"fits\", \"best\", \"dev\", \"haiku\", \"sonnet\", \"opus\", \"prompt\", \"matters\", \"must\", \"justify\", \"model\", \"choice\", \"client\", \"three\", \"things\", \"reason\", \"cover\", \"dev\", \"quality\", \"latency\", \"cost\", \"quality\", \"popularity\", \"age\", \"cost\", \"colour\", \"region\", \"latency\", \"brand\", \"licence\", \"script\", \"used\", \"hardcoded\", \"model\", \"name\", \"year\", \"suddenly\", \"returns\", \"404\", \"likely\", \"cause\", \"dev\", \"api\", \"key\", \"expired\", \"model\", \"name\", \"retired\", \"misspelled\", \"hit\", \"rate\", \"limit\", \"json\", \"malformed\", \"field\", \"reply\", \"tells\", \"many\", \"tokens\", \"call\", \"used\", \"dev\", \"content\", \"stop\", \"reason\", \"usage\", \"user\", \"complains\", \"claude\", \"answer\", \"stopped\"