", \"rules\", \"topics\", \"must\", \"refuse\", \"user\", \"current\", \"question\", \"client\", \"asks\", \"just\", \"use\", \"opus\", \"everything\", \"strongest\", \"answer\", \"dev\", \"opus\", \"less\", \"accurate\", \"opus\", \"use\", \"tools\", \"tasks\", \"need\", \"costs\", \"takes\", \"far\", \"gain\", \"opus\", \"research\", \"itwine\", \"technologies\", \"claude\", \"certification\", \"test\", \"booklet\"]','[\"Team Tests\", \"On Anthropic\", \"Claude Certification Test Booklet\"]','[\"8 October\"]','2026-10-08 12:12:08'),(11,1,1,8,8,'16 What does the Console playground (called the Workbench in older guides) let you do? DEV D2 A) Deploy to production B) Test prompts without writing code C) Edit your billing D) Train a model 17 You are designing an assistant for a client\'s website. Which of these is an architecture decision, not a prompt decision? ARCH D1 A) The assistant\'s tone B) Where the conversation history is stored C) The refusal wording D) The greeting text 18 Your system prompt says \"never discuss pricing\", but Claude discusses pricing when the user insists. What do you do first? DEV D7 A) Switch to a bigger model B) Tighten and retest the system prompt, then add a code-level check C) Lower max_tokens D) Tell the user not to ask 19 Which is true about a Workspace in the Developer Console? DEV D2 A) It is the same as an API key B) It groups keys, usage and limits, and we use one per client project C) It stores conversation history D) It is only for billing 20 You need the exam guide for your track. Where do you get it? BOTH A) Pearson VUE B) The Anthropic Partner Academy C) The Developer Console D) GitHub iTWINE Technologies · Claude Certification Test Booklet 9 / 19','[\"console\", \"playground\", \"called\", \"workbench\", \"older\", \"guides\", \"let\", \"dev\", \"deploy\", \"production\", \"test\", \"prompts\", \"without\", \"writing\", \"code\", \"edit\", \"billing\", \"train\", \"model\", \"designing\", \"assistant\", \"client\", \"website\", \"architecture\", \"decision\", \"prompt\", \"decision\", \"arch\", \"assistant\", \"tone\", \"conversation\", \"history\", \"stored\", \"refusal\", \"wording\", \"greeting\", \"text\", \"system\", \"prompt\", \"says\", \"never\", \"discuss\", \"pricing\", \"claude\", \"discusses\", \"pricing\", \"user\", \"insists\", \"first\", \"dev\", \"switch\", \"bigger\", \"model\", \"tighten\", \"retest\", \"system\", \"prompt\", \"add\", \"code\", \"level\", \"check\", \"lower\", \"max\", \"tokens\", \"tell\", \"user\", \"ask\", \"true\", \"workspace\", \"developer\", \"console\", \"dev\", \"api\", \"key\", \"groups\", \"keys\", \"usage\", \"limits\", \"use\", \"one\", \"per\", \"client\", \"project\", \"stores\", \"conversation\", \"history\", \"billing\", \"need\", \"exam\", \"guide\", \"track\", \"get\", \"pearson\", \"vue\", \"anthropic\", \"partner\", \"academy\", \"developer\", \"console\", \"github\", \"itwine\", \"technologies\", \"claude\", \"certification\", \"test\", \"booklet\"]','[\"Developer Console\", \"The Anthropic Partner Academy\", \"The Developer Console\", \"Claude Certification Test Booklet\"]','[]','2026-10-08 12:12:08'),(12,1,1,8,9,'Test #2 · Friday 16 October · Clean output, examples, long conversations, grounding, caching 1 You ask for JSON and Claude keeps adding \"Here is the JSON you asked for:\" before it. What is the most reliable fix? DEV D6 A) Ask more politely B) Use structured outputs or force a tool call C) Raise max_tokens D) Switch to Opus 2 How should you check that a reply is valid JSON? DEV D6 A) Read it carefully B) Ask Claude if it is valid C) Parse it in code and handle the failure D) Count the brackets 3 You add three examples to a prompt. Accuracy goes up. What else has changed? DEV D5 A) Nothing B) Every call now costs more input tokens C) The model changed D) The context window grew 4 Which set of three examples teaches the model most? DEV D6 A) Three easy cases B) Three identical cases C) Two easy cases and one difficult edge case D) Three cases with no expected output shown 5 Why wrap examples in XML tags? ARCH D4 A) It reduces token cost B) It makes the boundary between instruction and example clear C) It is required by the API D) It enables caching 6 A conversation is about to exceed the context window. Which is not a valid remedy? ARCH D5 A) Compaction B) Context editing C) Retrieving only the relevant documents D) Raising max_tokens 7 What is the difference between caching and retrieval? ARCH D5 A) None B) Caching reuses identical text you already sent; retrieval fetches new relevant text C) Caching is for images only D) Retrieval is cheaper than caching in all cases 8 Your trimming function silently drops the last 40 records of a long list. What is the main risk? DEV D6 A) Higher cost B) The model answers confidently using incomplete data, and nobody knows C) A 429 error D) A slower reply 9 You want Claude to refuse when the answer is not in the supplied text. What is the strongest instruction? DEV D7 A) \"Try not to guess\" B) \"Be accurate\" C) \"If the answer is not in the text above, output exactly: I don\'t know\" D) \"Say you are unsure\" 10 Which is stronger evidence that an answer is grounded in the source? ARCH D4 A) A confidence score the model produced B) The exact quoted sentence from the source C) A longer answer D) A lower temperature 11 Which field proves a cache hit really happened? DEV D5 A) cache_creation_input_tokens is 0 B) cache_read_input_tokens is above 0 C) input_tokens is 0 D) stop_reason is end_turn 12 Your cache never hits. Which of these would not explain it? DEV D5 A) The cached text is below the minimum length B) A timestamp changes inside the cached section C) You switched model between calls D) The user asked a different question after the cache point 13 Where should the cache breakpoint go in a document-processing app? ARCH D5 A) After the document, so the document is cached B) After the fixed instructions and before the document C) At the very start of the request D) Caching cannot be used with documents 14 Caching costs a little more to write and much less to read. What follows from that? DEV D5 A) Cache everything B) Only cache text you will reuse many times C) Never cache D) Cache the user\'s question 15 A two-pass extraction design means: ARCH D4 A) Sending the same prompt twice and comparing B) One call extracts, a second call checks the extraction against the source C) Using two models at once D) Retrying on failure 16 Which is the safest behaviour when a field cannot be read from a scanned document? DEV D7 A) Guess the most likely value B) Copy the value from the previous document C) Leave it blank and flag the document for a human D) Return zero 17 What does \"compaction\" do? ARCH D5 A) Compresses the API response B) Shortens earlier conversation history so the conversation can continue C) Removes tools from the request D) Reduces the model size iTWINE Technologies · Claude Certification Test Booklet 10 / 19','[\"test\", \"friday\", \"october\", \"clean\", \"output\", \"examples\", \"long\", \"conversations\", \"grounding\", \"caching\", \"ask\", \"json\", \"claude\", \"keeps\", \"adding\", \"json\", \"asked\", \"reliable\", \"fix\", \"dev\", \"ask\", \"politely\", \"use\", \"structured\", \"outputs\", \"force\", \"tool\", \"call\", \"raise\", \"max\", \"tokens\", \"switch\", \"opus\", \"check\", \"reply\", \"valid\", \"json\", \"dev\", \"read\", \"carefully\", \"ask\", \"claude\", \"valid\", \"parse\", \"code\", \"handle\", \"failure\", \"count\", \"brackets\", \"add\", \"three\", \"examples\", \"prompt\", \"accuracy\", \"goes\", \"else\", \"changed\", \"dev\", \"nothing\", \"every\", \"call\", \"now\", \"costs\", \"input\", \"tokens\", \"model\", \"changed\", \"context\", \"window\", \"grew\", \"set\", \"three\", \"examples\", \"teaches\", \"model\", \"dev\", \"three\", \"easy\", \"cases\", \"three\", \"identical\", \"cases\", \"two\", \"easy\", \"cases\", \"one\", \"difficult\", \"edge\", \"