ion for developers B) Telling Claude when to use the tool C) The error message D) The function name 4 Your supplier lookup service returns 503. What is the best tool_result to send back? DEV D4 A) An empty result B) A made-up supplier code C) is_error: true with an instruction on what to do instead D) Nothing; end the conversation 5 What must match between a tool_use block and its tool_result? DEV D8 A) The model name B) The tool_use_id C) The timestamp D) The token count 6 When is forcing a specific tool with tool_choice a bad idea? DEV D8 A) When you need a guaranteed output shape B) When the request might legitimately need no tool at all C) When there is only one tool D) It is never a bad idea 7 A tool schema declares a required parameter but the type is wrong. What error do you expect? DEV D4 A) 400 B) 401 C) 429 D) 529 8 Which statement about tool execution is correct? DEV D8 A) Claude executes the function on Anthropic\'s servers B) Claude asks for the function to be run and your application runs it C) The MCP server runs all tools including local ones D) Tools run inside the model 9 Your tool returns 4,000 records. What is the risk of passing them all back? ARCH D2 A) A 401 error B) You may blow the context window and the token budget C) Claude will refuse D) The tool_use_id changes 10 A tool fails and Claude invents a plausible answer instead. What was most likely missing? DEV D7 A) A bigger model B) is_error plus an instruction on what to do when the tool fails C) Streaming D) A longer timeout 11 Which is an architecture decision rather than a coding detail? ARCH D1 A) The variable name for the tool result B) Which failures we retry silently and which we show the user C) The indentation style D) The log file name 12 You cache your tool definitions. What must be true for the cache to keep working? DEV D5 A) The tool list must be byte-identical every call B) You must use Opus C) The tools must be under 5 in number D) You must disable streaming 13 What is the difference between an agent and a workflow? ARCH D1 A) None B) An agent decides its own next step; a workflow follows steps you fixed in advance C) A workflow is always faster D) An agent cannot use tools 14 A task has three fixed steps that never change. What should you build? ARCH D1 A) A multi-agent system B) A workflow C) A chatbot D) An MCP server 15 What does a good tool description include? DEV D8 A) The function\'s return type only B) When to use it, when not to use it, and what each parameter means C) The author\'s name D) The database schema 16 You return a tool_result but Claude repeats the same tool call. What is the most likely cause? DEV D4 A) A mismatched tool_use_id or a result Claude could not use B) A 429 error C) The cache expired D) The model is too small iTWINE Technologies · Claude Certification Test Booklet 12 / 19','[\"test\", \"wednesday\", \"october\", \"tool\", \"use\", \"put\", \"tool\", \"use\", \"loop\", \"right\", \"order\", \"dev\", \"user\", \"prompt\", \"code\", \"runs\", \"tool\", \"claude\", \"sends\", \"tool\", \"use\", \"final\", \"answer\", \"user\", \"prompt\", \"claude\", \"sends\", \"tool\", \"use\", \"code\", \"runs\", \"tool\", \"code\", \"sends\", \"tool\", \"result\", \"final\", \"answer\", \"claude\", \"runs\", \"tool\", \"returns\", \"answer\", \"user\", \"prompt\", \"tool\", \"result\", \"tool\", \"use\", \"final\", \"answer\", \"claude\", \"keeps\", \"choosing\", \"wrong\", \"one\", \"two\", \"similar\", \"tools\", \"fix\", \"arch\", \"system\", \"prompt\", \"model\", \"tool\", \"descriptions\", \"schema\", \"max\", \"tokens\", \"tool\", \"description\", \"field\", \"actually\", \"dev\", \"documentation\", \"developers\", \"telling\", \"claude\", \"use\", \"tool\", \"error\", \"message\", \"function\", \"name\", \"supplier\", \"lookup\", \"service\", \"returns\", \"503\", \"best\", \"tool\", \"result\", \"send\", \"back\", \"dev\", \"empty\", \"result\", \"made\", \"supplier\", \"code\", \"error\", \"true\", \"instru