ata\", \"intend\", \"review\", \"expose\", \"connecting\", \"used\", \"production\", \"run\", \"inside\", \"model\", \"retries\", \"create\", \"duplicate\", \"erp\", \"entries\", \"property\", \"missing\", \"dev\", \"statelessness\", \"idempotency\", \"streaming\", \"caching\", \"itwine\", \"technologies\", \"claude\", \"certification\", \"test\", \"booklet\"]','[\"Claude Certification Test Booklet\"]','[]','2026-10-08 12:12:09'),(18,1,1,8,15,'Test #5 · Friday 13 November Everyone answers questions 1 to 15. Then Developers answer D1 to D5, and Architects answer A1 to A5. Twenty questions in total. Questions 1 to 15 — everyone 1 When is the Message Batches API the right choice? DEV D2 A) A live chat window B) A nightly job where nobody is waiting C) A fraud check that must answer in 200ms D) Any request over 1,000 tokens 2 Which is not a reason to choose batch over live? DEV D5 A) Lower cost B) High volume C) No one waiting for the answer D) Higher accuracy 3 What is the point of giving a subagent a very limited view of the information? ARCH D1 A) Speed B) Cost C) Keeping it focused and stopping information leaking where it should not go D) It is a technical limit 4 In a hub-and-spoke design, what does the main agent do? ARCH D1 A) Runs all the tools itself B) Splits the task and gives work to subagents, then combines the results C) Stores the conversation D) Handles billing 5 Which task needs no agent at all? ARCH D1 A) Researching a topic across many sources B) Translating one paragraph C) Debugging a codebase D) Planning a multi-step migration 6 What does streaming change about error handling? DEV D2 A) Nothing B) Part of the answer may already be on the user\'s screen when the failure happens C) Errors stop being returned D) It removes the need for retries 7 How do you send a scanned PDF to Claude? DEV D2 A) As a URL only B) As base64 with the correct media type C) As plain text D) Through the MCP registry 8 A six-page scan fails with 413. What has happened? DEV D4 A) Wrong API key B) Rate limit C) The request is larger than the allowed size D) The model is retired 9 When is extended thinking worth its extra cost? DEV D5 A) On every request B) On simple classification C) On genuinely hard reasoning problems D) When latency matters most 10 Why should model names live in a settings file rather than in the code? DEV D2 A) It looks tidier B) So there is one place to change them when a model is retired C) It is faster D) The API requires it 11 Why version your prompts like code? DEV D2 A) To use less memory B) So you can tell which prompt produced which result, and roll back C) The API requires it D) It improves caching 12 Which is the correct retry strategy for 429? DEV D2 A) Retry instantly B) Fixed 3-second wait C) Longer wait after each attempt, plus a random delay D) Do not retry at all 13 The same feature is built as a chat window and as a nightly batch job. What is most likely to differ? DEV D2 A) The model family, the error handling and whether a human reviews B) Only the colour scheme C) Nothing D) The API key 14 What is the first question to answer in any new Claude project? DEV D2 A) Which model? B) What must the system never do without a human? C) Which framework? D) What is the budget? 15 A client asks for full automation with no human review. What is the professional answer? ARCH D1 A) Agree; the client knows best B) Refuse the project C) Propose a value limit and an uncertainty rule, so only safe cases are automatic D) Use a bigger model instead Questions D1 to D5 — Developer track only D1 Which sub-topic carries the most marks on the Developer exam? DEV D2 A) Claude Code B) Claude application design C) Debugging D) MCP server development iTWINE Technologies · Claude Certification Test Booklet 16 / 19','[\"test\", \"friday\", \"november\", \"everyone\", \"answers\", \"questions\", \"developers\", \"answer\", \"architects\", \"answer\", \"twenty\", \"questions\", \"total\", \"questions\", \"everyone\", \"message\",