 At the end of the session D4 You must process 400 documents per week with a two-hour turnaround and the lowest cost. What do you choose? DEV D5 A) Live calls with Opus B) Batch with Sonnet, and Haiku for the first classification step C) Streaming with Opus D) Live calls with Haiku only D5 Your batch submission succeeds. What must your code do next? DEV D2 A) Nothing; results arrive by email B) Poll the status endpoint until processing is complete, then fetch the results C) Resend the batch D) Open a websocket Questions A1 to A5 — Architect track only A1 Which topic carries the most marks on the Architect exam? ARCH D1 A) Context Management B) Claude Code Configuration C) Agentic Architecture and Orchestration D) Prompt Engineering A2 Claude Code settings can come from the user, the project and the company. Why does the order matter? ARCH D3 A) It affects speed B) It decides which setting wins when two of them disagree C) It changes the model D) It does not matter A3 What is CLAUDE.md for? ARCH D3 A) Documentation for new hires B) Project rules that a Claude Code agent reads and follows C) The changelog D) The licence A4 What should Claude Code never be allowed to do inside an automatic build pipeline? ARCH D3 A) Read files B) Run tests C) Push to a shared branch or call a production endpoint D) Write a summary A5 What does /compact do to a Claude Code session? ARCH D3 A) Deletes the session B) Shortens the earlier history so the session can continue C) Compresses the files on disk D) Reduces the model size iTWINE Technologies · Claude Certification Test Booklet 17 / 19','[\"agent\", \"sdk\", \"give\", \"plain\", \"api\", \"call\", \"dev\", \"cheaper\", \"model\", \"loop\", \"subagents\", \"hooks\", \"tool\", \"wiring\", \"already\", \"built\", \"user\", \"interface\", \"free\", \"tokens\", \"write\", \"posttooluse\", \"hook\", \"run\", \"dev\", \"model\", \"called\", \"tool\", \"used\", \"errors\", \"end\", \"session\", \"must\", \"process\", \"400\", \"documents\"