you to book the real exam. A second version runs on Tuesday 1 December. Run this one on paper, in one room, with a clock. How to build it — for whoever is organising The Gateway Test is assembled from the question banks in this document, plus a small number of new questions. Build both versions in the week beginning 16 November. Part Where the questions come from How many Notes A Tests #1 to #5 in Sections 4 and 5 of this booklet 30 Pick them by topic weight, using the table below. Do not pick 6 from each test — pick 30 that match the shape of the real exam. B The starting test in Section 3 5 These check the basics have stuck. If someone still gets these wrong in November, that is important to know. C New questions written from Appendix G of the Study Plan 10 Write short work situations based on PO-01 and ask which design choice is best. This is the format the real exam uses most. D New questions from the weak-spot boxes 5 Read the team\'s weak-spot boxes from Weeks 1 to 7 and write five questions on whatever appears most often. How many questions from each topic Match the real exam\'s shape. Round to whole questions. Developer version (CCDV-F) Q Architect version (CCAR-F) Q D2 Applications and Integration 17 D1 Agentic Architecture 14 D5 Model Selection and Optimisation 8 D3 Claude Code Configuration 10 D1 Agents and Workflows 7 D4 Prompt Engineering and Structured Output 10 D6 Prompt and Context Engineering 6 D2 Tool Design and MCP Integration 9 D8 Tools and MCPs 5 D5 Context Management 7 D7 Security and Safety 4 D3 Claude Code 2 D4 Eval, Testing and Debugging 1 Total 50 Total 50 Rules on the day Ninety minutes. No notes, no documentation, no AI help. Phones away. 1 Everyone takes it at the same time, alone. 2 iTWINE Technologies · Claude Certification Test Booklet 18 / 19','[\"section\", \"gateway\", \"test\", \"fifty\", \"questions\", \"monday\", \"november\", \"clears\", \"book\", \"real\", \"exam\", \"second\", \"version\", \"runs\", \"tuesday\", \"december\",